{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"2ddb90595ab22787","name":"card_unit_216th_guards","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Soviet/OceaniaStorm/units/card_unit_216th_guards","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"216th GUARDS","text":"At the start of your turn, deal 2 damage to your HQ and draw a card. Becomes Veteran after the second time.","flavorText":"The 216th Guards Rifle Regiment began as the 1043rd Rifle Regiment of the 284th Rifle Division. Its Guards title was earned at the Battle of Stalingrad, where the division held positions around Mamayev Kurgan and parts of the city center against the German Sixth Army. In March 1943, the 284th was redesignated as the 79th Guards Rifle Division, and the 1043rd became the 216th Guards Rifle Regiment. The regiment later distinguished itself during the Vistula crossing in 1944. Near Magnuszew, the division forced the river crossing under pressure, and the 1st Battalion of the 216th Guards was among the first units to succeed. Its commander, Captain Yefim Tsitovsky, was named a Hero of the Soviet Union for his role in securing the bridgehead. The 79th Guards Rifle Division kept fighting westward through Ukraine, Poland, and Germany as part of the 8th Guards Army. It earned the honorific “Zaporozhye” after the capture of the city in 1943, then participated in the Battles of the Oder, Seelow Heights, and Berlin. In the final push, it crossed the Teltow Canal and helped capture Tempelhof Airfield.","faction":"Soviet","type":"infantry","rarity":"Common","cost":3,"operationCost":1,"attack":3,"defense":5},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_216th_guards","title":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_216th_guards_title","SourceString":"216th GUARDS","LocalizedString":"216th GUARDS"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":3,"defense":5,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Soviet","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_216th_guards_text","SourceString":"At the start of your turn, deal 2 damage to your HQ and draw a card. Becomes Veteran after the second time.","LocalizedString":"At the start of your turn, deal 2 damage to your HQ and draw a card. Becomes Veteran after the second time."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_216th_guards_history","SourceString":"The 216th Guards Rifle Regiment began as the 1043rd Rifle Regiment of the 284th Rifle Division. Its Guards title was earned at the Battle of Stalingrad, where the division held positions around Mamayev Kurgan and parts of the city center against the German Sixth Army. In March 1943, the 284th was redesignated as the 79th Guards Rifle Division, and the 1043rd became the 216th Guards Rifle Regiment. The regiment later distinguished itself during the Vistula crossing in 1944. Near Magnuszew, the division forced the river crossing under pressure, and the 1st Battalion of the 216th Guards was among the first units to succeed. Its commander, Captain Yefim Tsitovsky, was named a Hero of the Soviet Union for his role in securing the bridgehead. The 79th Guards Rifle Division kept fighting westward through Ukraine, Poland, and Germany as part of the 8th Guards Army. It earned the honorific “Zaporozhye” after the capture of the city in 1943, then participated in the Battles of the Oder, Seelow Heights, and Berlin. In the final push, it crossed the Teltow Canal and helped capture Tempelhof Airfield.","LocalizedString":"The 216th Guards Rifle Regiment began as the 1043rd Rifle Regiment of the 284th Rifle Division. Its Guards title was earned at the Battle of Stalingrad, where the division held positions around Mamayev Kurgan and parts of the city center against the German Sixth Army. In March 1943, the 284th was redesignated as the 79th Guards Rifle Division, and the 1043rd became the 216th Guards Rifle Regiment. The regiment later distinguished itself during the Vistula crossing in 1944. Near Magnuszew, the division forced the river crossing under pressure, and the 1st Battalion of the 216th Guards was among the first units to succeed. Its commander, Captain Yefim Tsitovsky, was named a Hero of the Soviet Union for his role in securing the bridgehead. The 79th Guards Rifle Division kept fighting westward through Ukraine, Poland, and Germany as part of the 8th Guards Army. It earned the honorific “Zaporozhye” after the capture of the city in 1943, then participated in the Battles of the Oder, Seelow Heights, and Berlin. In the final push, it crossed the Teltow Canal and helped capture Tempelhof Airfield."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::OceaniaStorm","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnStartofTurn"],"spawnCardName":"card_unit_216th_guards_vet","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/216th_GUARDS.216th_GUARDS","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_216th_guards_photo","SourceString":"Red Army infantry crossing the Vistula river in 1944. ","LocalizedString":"Red Army infantry crossing the Vistula river in 1944. "},"blowUpExplosionNiagara":{"ObjectName":"NiagaraSystem'NS_ExplosionInfantryM'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Effects/Niagara/NS_ExplosionInfantryM.46"},"blowUpCameraShake":{"ObjectName":"BlueprintGeneratedClass'CameraShakeMedium_C'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/examples/GrenadePack/Blueprints/CameraShakeMedium.0"},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/Infantry/BP_AttackInfantry.BP_AttackInfantry_C","SubPathString":""},"isDefenseBuff":true},"variables":[],"functions":[{"name":"ExecuteUbergraph_card_unit_216th_guards","owner":"card_unit_216th_guards_C","params":[{"name":"EntryPoint","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"pure":false,"event":false,"flags":"FUNC_Final | FUNC_UbergraphFunction | FUNC_HasDefaults","locals":[{"name":"Temp_int_Array_Index_Variable","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"Temp_int_Loop_Counter_Variable","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name"